# Edit-crochet keypad (authoritative spec)

The keypad owns a draft of the **whole row** plus a cursor `containerPath` (indices into nested
`pattern` / `bundle` nodes; `[]` = row root). All edits go through pure helpers in
`src/utils/keypadEdit.js`; EditCrochet emits `{ list, replaceWholeRow: true }` on every change.

## Sections
- **Stitch** — always shown. Inserts at the caret (insertion point) in the current container.
- **Pattern** (`重複花樣`) — appends an empty pattern ×1 and moves into it.
  Shown at the root, or inside a pattern **that already has children** (rule 1). Hidden in a bundle.
- **Same stitch** (`在同一針目裡`) — appends an empty bundle (consume 1) and moves into it.
  Inside a bundle only the Stitch section is shown.

## Input display
- Shows the whole row; the current pattern/bundle has the yellow highlight, the rest is normal.
- The current **pattern or bundle** always shows `× n` (InputNumber) right after it. The root has no ×.
- Clicking any node selects the **deepest pattern or bundle containing it** (both are containers with a child list, so they are selected the same way); outside both nothing happens.

## Navigation
- While a pattern/bundle is selected, the bottom bar's 取消/儲存 become a single **確認** (`confirmSelection`): it goes to the parent level; leaving an empty container removes it. At the root the normal 取消/儲存 show. There is no last-page button.
- Caret: index 0…childCount inside the current container (`KeypadCaret`, moved with the `KeypadCaretButton` ◀ (left of the input display) / ▶ (right of it, before delete) or by tapping a direct child). It never leaves the current container; inserts go at the caret, entering a container puts it at 0 (new) or the end (tapped), 確認 puts it right after the container left.
- Delete (backspace): removes the node before the caret; at the start of an empty container removes it and goes to the parent.
- Save prunes empty patterns/bundles (`pruneEmptyContainers`).

The root is never a pattern. There is no "change stitch" / "add to bundle" selection mode.
